WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.698
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:05.998 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:16.749
Unit fifteen: Common Phrasal Verbs. Today you will understand and use phrasal verbs from daily life and school.

4
00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:19.864
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.149
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.135
Phrasal verb.

7
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.438
Phrasal verb means a verb with a small word like up or off.

8
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.829
Give up is a phrasal verb.

9
00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:36.533
Your turn. Say: Phrasal verb.

10
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.796
Phrasal verb.

11
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.400
Give up.

12
00:00:43.417 --> 00:00:45.149
Give up means to stop trying.

13
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:46.948
Never give up.

14
00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.063
Your turn. Say: Give up.

15
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:53.646
Give up.

16
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:55.408
Look for.

17
00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:58.265
Look for means to search for.

18
00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.478
I am looking for my book.

19
00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:03.596
Your turn. Say: Look for.

20
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.353
Look for.

21
00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:08.955
Turn on.

22
00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.042
Turn on means to start a machine.

23
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:13.698
Turn on the light.

24
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:16.483
Your turn. Say: Turn on.

25
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:20.125
Turn on.

26
00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:21.803
Turn off.

27
00:01:22.817 --> 00:01:24.735
Turn off means to stop a machine.

28
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.676
Turn off the fan.

29
00:01:27.283 --> 00:01:29.460
Your turn. Say: Turn off.

30
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.080
Turn off.

31
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:34.748
Take off.

32
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.446
Take off means to remove clothes or leave the ground.

33
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.504
Take off your shoes.

34
00:01:41.117 --> 00:01:43.804
Your turn. Say: Take off.

35
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.610
Take off.

36
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.142
Get up.

37
00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.010
Get up means to leave your bed.

38
00:01:52.617 --> 00:01:53.989
I get up at six.

39
00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:56.481
Your turn. Say: Get up.

40
00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:00.044
Get up.

41
00:02:00.783 --> 00:02:01.773
Find out.

42
00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:05.038
Find out means to discover information.

43
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.336
I want to find out the answer.

44
00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.579
Your turn. Say: Find out.

45
00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.388
Find out.

46
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.793
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.789
Visal, what are phrasal verbs?

48
00:02:22.883 --> 00:02:34.882
They are verbs with small words such as up, off, on or out, and the meaning is often different from the verb alone. For example, give up means stop trying.

49
00:02:35.983 --> 00:02:37.205
How do I learn them?

50
00:02:38.317 --> 00:02:51.702
Learn them in sentences and by topic. Daily life: get up, turn on and turn off. Study: look up, find out and hand in. Feelings: cheer up and calm down.

51
00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:54.549
Can the words be separated?

52
00:02:55.650 --> 00:03:06.371
Some can: Turn the light on, or Turn on the light. But when we use a pronoun, we must separate it: Turn it on, not Turn on it.

53
00:03:07.533 --> 00:03:09.010
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:13.672
Grammar focus: Phrasal verb: verb plus particle.

55
00:03:13.972 --> 00:03:15.217
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:17.730
I get up at six every morning.

57
00:03:18.617 --> 00:03:20.570
Please turn it off before you leave.

58
00:03:21.533 --> 00:03:27.878
Learn phrasal verbs as whole phrases in sentences. With pronouns, put the pronoun between the verb and the particle.

59
00:03:28.617 --> 00:03:31.397
Be careful! Don't say: Turn off it.

60
00:03:33.333 --> 00:03:34.973
Say: Turn it off.

61
00:03:35.273 --> 00:03:36.657
Pronoun goes in the middle.

62
00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.910
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.875
A Busy Morning.

64
00:03:42.175 --> 00:03:44.639
Sovann gets up at six every morning.

65
00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:48.341
He turns on the light and looks for his school bag.

66
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:51.832
He finds out that he has forgotten his homework.

67
00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:55.228
He doesn't give up, and he finishes it quickly.

68
00:03:56.233 --> 00:03:58.500
Before he leaves, he turns off the fan.

69
00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.695
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.853
Give up means blank.

71
00:04:06.153 --> 00:04:09.830
A, stop trying. B, start. C, sleep.

72
00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.297
The answer is A: stop trying.

73
00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:19.265
Turn blank the light, please. (start it)

74
00:04:19.565 --> 00:04:22.464
A, over. B, on. C, off.

75
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.209
The answer is B: on.

76
00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:30.572
Which is correct?

77
00:04:30.872 --> 00:04:34.699
A, Turn off it.. B, Off turn it.. C, Turn it off..

78
00:04:38.233 --> 00:04:40.709
The answer is C: Turn it off..

79
00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.513
What does Sovann look for?

80
00:04:43.813 --> 00:04:47.966
A, his school bag. B, a taxi. C, a book shop.

81
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.709
The answer is A: his school bag.

82
00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.246
Find out means blank.

83
00:04:56.546 --> 00:05:00.768
A, forget. B, discover information. C, hide.

84
00:05:04.333 --> 00:05:06.855
The answer is B: discover information.

85
00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:11.114
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.588
Tell me about your morning using phrasal verbs.

87
00:05:23.383 --> 00:05:24.756
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:25.056 --> 00:05:34.781
I get up at six and turn on the light. Then I look for my school uniform and take off my pyjamas. Before I leave, I turn off the fan.

89
00:05:35.081 --> 00:05:37.046
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:43.458
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and phrasal verb: verb plus particle.

91
00:05:43.758 --> 00:05:47.932
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

92
00:05:48.232 --> 00:05:50.872
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:51.172 --> 00:05:53.709
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

